[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.760]   As a reminder, the Rule of 40 is an industry rule of thumb that says a high-growth SaaS
[00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:09.420]   company can burn as much cash as it likes in order to drive growth, as long as its growth
[00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.680]   rate is 40 percentage points higher than its free cash flow margin.
[00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.720]   It's an attempt at devising a simple rule to help software companies with the complex
[00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.680]   question of how to balance growth and profitability.
[00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.880]   One past study showed that while Rule of 40 compliant software companies made up a little
[00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.480]   more than half of all public software companies that they captured more than 80% of all public
[00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:29.180]   market cap.
